  "id": "Hackney-2024_2560",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;The proposed windows and door, by reason of their detailed design, specifically the frame proportions. glazing bars and the appearance of the uPVC &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space-collapse: preserve; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;would fail to preserve the character and appearance of the host building and the terrace it forms part of, thereby having an adverse impact on the visual amenities of the street scene.&amp;nbsp; It would, therefore, be contrary to policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020) and policies D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) and D4 (Delivering good design) of the London Plan (2021) and the SPD Residential Extensions and Alterations (2009).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
